</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib24" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Wu et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Yiwei Wu, Atticus Geiger, and Raphaël Millière.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">How do transformers learn variable binding in symbolic programs?

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <em id="bib.bib24.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Forty-second International Conference on Machine Learning</em>, 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=kVtyv7bpnw" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://openreview.net/forum?id=kVtyv7bpnw</a>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>List of Binding Tasks</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define ten different binding tasks spanning domains, syntaxes, and subjects: one with <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math> and nine with <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math>. Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix A List of Binding Tasks ‣ Mixing Mechanisms: How Language Models Retrieve Bound Entities In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists the entity sets for each task, along with an example instantiation for <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> and different values of <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\text{entity}}{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\text{entity}}{}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that when <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math>, we use two query entities: <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{q_{\text{entity}}{}^{1}}^{q_{\text{group}}{}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext>group</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{q_{\text{entity}}{}^{1}}^{q_{\text{group}}{}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{q_{\text{entity}}{}^{2}}^{q_{\text{group}}{}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext>group</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{q_{\text{entity}}{}^{2}}^{q_{\text{group}}{}}</annotation></semantics></math>. These are the two entities in the entity group which aren’t the target entity. For example, when <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}=2</annotation></semantics></math> we set <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\text{entity}}{}^{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\text{entity}}{}^{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\text{entity}}{}^{2}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\text{entity}}{}^{2}=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ B.2 Encoding of Positional Information ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ Mixing Mechanisms: How Language Models Retrieve Bound Entities In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ B.2 Encoding of Positional Information ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ Mixing Mechanisms: How Language Models Retrieve Bound Entities In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> show the results of the <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="15.68" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-5.15px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 94.09 15.68" width="94.09"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,15.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.84 L 0 10.84 C 0 13.51 2.17 15.68 4.84 15.68 L 89.25 15.68 C 91.92 15.68 94.09 13.51 94.09 10.84 L 94.09 4.84 C 94.09 2.17 91.92 0 89.25 0 L 4.84 0 C 2.17 0 0 2.17 0 4.84 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#ECECEC;" fill="#ECECEC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.84 L 0.69 10.84 C 0.69 13.13 2.55 14.99 4.84 14.99 L 89.25 14.99 C 91.54 14.99 93.4 13.13 93.4 10.84 L 93.4 4.84 C 93.4 2.55 91.54 0.69 89.25 0.69 L 4.84 0.69 C 2.55 0.69 0.69 2.55 0.69 4.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 3.46 5.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10.5pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.46)" width="87.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TargetRebind</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span> interchange intervention on gemma-2-2b-it and qwen2.5-7b-it across all tasks and all values of <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our findings are consistent: the positional mechanism dominates for early and late entity groups, while the lexical and reflexive mechanisms take over in the middle. We also replicate the effect in Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Prior Studies of Entity Binding in LMs ‣ 2 Problem Setup and Prior Work ‣ Mixing Mechanisms: How Language Models Retrieve Bound Entities In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Takeaways ‣ 3.3 Intervention Experiments ‣ 3 Three Mechanisms for Retrieving Bound Entities ‣ Mixing Mechanisms: How Language Models Retrieve Bound Entities In-Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>: reflexive is more present when <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (first), lexical when <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}=3</annotation></semantics></math> (last), and both are balanced when <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}=2</annotation></semantics></math> (middle).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Name</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity Sets Sample</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T1.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Binding Example</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Filling Liquids</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">John</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Mary</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{cup},\textit{glass}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">cup</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">glass</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{cup},\textit{glass}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{wine},\textit{beer}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">wine</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">beer</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{wine},\textit{beer}\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T1.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">John and Mary are working at a busy restaurant. To fulfill an order, John fills a cup with beer and Mary fills a glass with wine. Who filled a cup with beer?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">People and Objects</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">John</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Mary</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{toy},\textit{medicine}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">toy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">medicine</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{toy},\textit{medicine}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{kitchen},\textit{office}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">kitchen</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">office</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{kitchen},\textit{office}\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T1.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">John put the cup in the office and Mary put the toy in the kitchen. What did Mary put in the kitchen?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Programming Dictionary</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{a},\textit{b}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">a</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">b</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{a},\textit{b}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">John</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Mary</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{US},\textit{Canada}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">US</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Canada</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{US},\textit{Canada}\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T1.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The following are dictionary variables in Python: a={‘name’:‘Mary’, ‘Country’:‘Canada’}, b={‘name’:‘John’, ‘Country’:‘US’}. What is the country in variable a where ‘name’ == ‘John’?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Music</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">John</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Mary</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{rock},\textit{pop}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">rock</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pop</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}=\{\textit{rock},\textit{pop}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A1.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{guitar},\textit{piano}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">guitar</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">piano</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{3}=\{\textit{guitar},\textit{piano}\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A1.T1.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">At the music festival, John performed rock music on the piano, and Mary performed pop music on the guitar. What music did Mary play on the guitar?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Biology Experiment</th>
<td id="A1.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T1.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T1.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">John</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Mary</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}=\{\textit{John},\textit{Mary}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
