entity in the counterfactual does not exist in the original. Right: results for non-lexical and reflexive patch effects under the <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.F26.pic4" class="ltx_picture" height="15.68" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-5.15px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 94.09 15.68" width="94.09"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,15.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.84 L 0 10.84 C 0 13.51 2.17 15.68 4.84 15.68 L 89.25 15.68 C 91.92 15.68 94.09 13.51 94.09 10.84 L 94.09 4.84 C 94.09 2.17 91.92 0 89.25 0 L 4.84 0 C 2.17 0 0 2.17 0 4.84 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#ECECEC;" fill="#ECECEC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.84 L 0.69 10.84 C 0.69 13.13 2.55 14.99 4.84 14.99 L 89.25 14.99 C 91.54 14.99 93.4 13.13 93.4 10.84 L 93.4 4.84 C 93.4 2.55 91.54 0.69 89.25 0.69 L 4.84 0.69 C 2.55 0.69 0.69 2.55 0.69 4.84 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 3.46 5.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10.5pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.46)" width="87.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.F26.pic4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TargetRebind</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span> interchange intervention on gemma-2-2b-it with <math id="A5.F26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{entity}}{}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>entity</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{entity}}{}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, where the queried entity in the counterfactual does not exist in the original. We can see that when the model can’t use the lexical and reflexive mechanisms, it falls back on the noisy positional mechanism.</figcaption>
</figure>
